RANDOM IDEAS TO IMPROVE DETECTION OR EXTEND TO OTHER ABILITIES -----------------
- nameplate personal buffs/debuffs
    - this could be a massive information source for IDing buffs that we'd like
      to track but didn't make it onto blizzard's IMPORTANT/BIG/EXTERNAL flag set.
    - need to test an ability that we wish could be tracked but isn't (like fort brew?)
- detect abilities that reset other cooldowns like adrenaline rush and ice block
    - should not be hard. if the ability has a fixed cooldown (i.e. no CDR),
      then seeing that ability before it is available means the reset was used,
      so infer the reset ability. can track the CD of that.
        * would not be able to track the reset ability if it was used to reset
          something else. e.g., if prep was used while adrenaline rush was available,
          the prep usage would not be noticed. but that's fine.
- UPDATE_STEALTH event for shadowmeld? should also look for leave-combat events like
    - PLAYER_REGEN_ENABLED (mentions "and player not on hate list of any NPC"..)
    - PLAYER_LEAVE_COMBAT (mentions leaves combat "through abilities")
- [maybe] add CCs/stops if the blizzard CC flags cause uniquely identifiable events
- do cheat death events generally fire IMPORTANT events? rogue, evoker, DH, warrior, mage..
- could hunter exhil be detected by the idea that they only have one
- GoAK might not be cancellable? check. helps identify.
    - it isn't. right clicking and /cancelaura do not work
    - however filter=HELPFUL|CANCELABLE is the same for ardent defender and GOAK,
      despite AD being cancelable (right click and /cancelaura)
