LIMITATIONS
===========================================================================
- Weird cases: like multiple paladins. Are their externals always different
  buffs or might they update? Sacs must be different since they deal damage
  to the casters, but what about freedoms?

- Re-application of buffs when inference fails (or is turned off) can't be
  detected. For example, if a charge>1 ability is pressed a second time while it's
  already running, we will miss the first use if it wasn't inferred (or the user
  disabled inference). the first use can't be distinguished from a buff that
  naturally updates itself (e.g., paladin sentinel) since inference doesn't know
  what's going on. in this case, only the second use will be sent to the history
  tray when it expires.

- Only history tray mode is available for other players that do not have LibSpec.
  LibSpec is embedded in common addons like bigwigs (and this addon), so many
  people will have it without knowing.

- Abilities with dynamic cooldown reduction (CDR) are hard to handle. This means
  abilities that reduce their cooldown due to some event - for example, a guardian
  druid's Incarn cooldown is reduced by 1 sec for for every 25 rage spent. Since these
  events can't (generally) be detected, the cooldown will show the MAXIMUM POSSIBLE
  (worst case) cooldown. This information can still be useful, but judgment is required.
    - For these reasons, there is an option to disable inference for abilities with
      dynamic CDR. They will instead always be sent to the history tray rather than
      display an inaccurate timer. This instead shows you **how long** it has been since
      the ability was last used.
    - A much bigger problem: abilities with **both** CDR and multiple charges. For
      multi-charge abilities, only one charge recharges at a time. If there is no
      dynamic CDR, this is no problem to track. But if there is CDR, consider the
      case where both charges are used back to back: because of CDR, we don't know
      when the first recharge finishes (equivalent to not knowing when a 1-charge
      ability with CDR comes off cooldown), which means we also don't know when the
      second ability **begins** charging. This compounding issue makes the cooldown info
      very difficult to judge.
        Rotational CDR (definitely not trackable)
        - disc priest: pain suppression
            - CDR on PW:S casts
        - prot pal: GoAK
            - CDR on holy power spenders
        - prot war: shield wall
            - CDR on rage use and shield slams
        CDR on large cooldowns (e.g., resets)
        * balance druid: incarn/celestial alignment
            - keeper of the grove talent that reduces cooldown based on time spent
              with ability off CD.
        * aug evoker: scales
            - potentially trackable since the CDR is attached to a long
              cooldown that may itself be trackable


KNOWN BUGS
===========================================================================
- Death handling is not implemented. For now, buffs that are running when the
  unit dies may not be inferred. Support will be added later.

- Changes to party sorting order aren't detected. If you change your
  party sort (e.g., edit mode > party frames > sort), you need to /reload for
  the cooldown trackers to update. There must be a way to handle this, but I don't
  know how.

- bug in libspec: when entering a follower dungeon with a role that doesn't match
  your spec, the game forces you into another spec (e.g., if a paladin queues for a
  follower dungeon as a DPS while prot, it forces the paladin's spec to ret).
  this forced respec does not trigger a new libspec callback. same when you leave the
  follower dungeon and it returns you to your previous spec. you must /reload for
  talents/abilities to be updated.

- frost mage: cold snap can reset ice cold/ice block, so expect to see these abilities
  occur sometimes when the mage has cold snap



